{"kind":"assert","text":"CUT-A2 read-only plan at current main 0ad4aa91. Small source surface: scripts/register-values.mjs, its existing owning scripts/register-values.test.mjs, and docs/deploy.md. Source starts only after corrected Head A and R1.\n\nUse one exported-helper option, mode: 'only' | 'keep'. The CLI recognizes both flags, requires exactly one, rejects both/repetition before reading the target, and returns that same mode to registerValuesSource. The helper independently rejects missing/invalid mode and retired only/keep boolean fields before parsing/loading validators, so automation cannot recover the old default or pass contradictory representations. --only always writes [newRoot]. --keep uses the validated installed roots plus the new root once, preserving order; without an explicit list the existing primary is the installed root that --keep explicitly retains. Existing production settings agreement, 32-root capacity, Start/deployment validation, JSONC preservation and coupled REGISTER_SCOPE/ARTIFACTS_CONFIG remain in their owners. The helper has only its in-file caller and two direct owning-test calls today; all will use mode explicitly. Every old refusal test must supply a valid mode unless mode itself is the subject, so the new guard cannot make those tests vacuous.\n\nFor file mode, observe the selected regular target's identity/mode beside its original bytes. Write the sibling pending candidate with exclusive creation, apply the observed permission bits with chmod before rename (creation mode alone is filtered by umask), and retain same-filesystem atomic rename. Compare final target bytes plus identity/mode again after diff output and pending preparation, immediately before rename. Current check at register-values.mjs:163 precedes write(diff), so an existing injectable output callback can deterministically edit the target after that check; the final check must catch that edit. Atomic replacement makes readers see one complete file. The final comparison catches preparation races; ordinary rename is not a compare-and-swap against an uncooperative concurrent writer, so the runbook must require the selected file to stay idle through replacement. This is an existing limitation, not a claim of lock-free serialization.\n\nUpdate the existing docs/deploy.md register-update section at314-354: make the general example explicitly choose --keep, describe both mandatory flags and mutual exclusion, and state that a listed root admits creation under that root. Preserve the existing cutover --only example and Start metadata rules. Place crash cleanup beside the write description: identify \u003cselected-config\u003e.register-values-\u003csuffix\u003e/candidate, confirm the run has stopped, inspect the selected config diff because rename may already have completed, then remove only that run's candidate and empty pending directory. No new command or old-default compatibility path.\n\nStrengthen the existing owner with four real temporary-Git success cases (only/keep × list/no-list), the explicit no-choice refusal naming both flags, both/repeated choices, direct-helper mode refusal, duplicate/idempotent keep, and a successful replacement preserving mode0640. Existing validation/dirty-file/other-tracked-bytes assertions remain meaningful. Add the controlled output-callback edit to require refusal without overwriting that later edit; it needs no new production hook. One exact-baseline control can run only the no-choice refusal witness on unchanged 0ad4aa91: its old default accepts the valid ordinary grow config and widens the list, so the control fails an actual exit/content assertion rather than an unknown --keep/API error. All tests/control and the required gate or approved follow-up remain UNRUN. No contract question needs a new ruling for this plan.","body":{"head":"0ad4aa9102fe5f75b692d3adb30c8b00a6914574","to":"planner","validation":"Read-only CUT-A2 plan. No source edits, compiler, test, formatter, model, generator, build, gate or deployment."}}